The issue lies in the devicetree node name `biometrics-emul` in the `app.overlay` file. While hyphens are valid in devicetree node names, Zephyr's build system and macros work more reliably with node names that are also valid C identifiers.

The fix is to change the node name from `biometrics-emul` to `biometrics_emul`, which uses an underscore instead of a hyphen. This change makes the node name a valid C identifier, ensuring it is correctly processed by the build system. The node's label `biometrics_emul` is already correct and is used by the alias, so no other changes are needed.

